---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="GEAR Moto Foundation's commitment to improving website accessibility, current limitations and a way to report problems.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">All Bikes / All Riders</div><h1>ACCESS FOR<br/><span class="accent">EVERY RIDER.</span></h1><p class="lede" style="color:#e5e8eb">Everyone should be able to understand our mission and reach us.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
<div class="program-callout"><strong>Accessibility review is ongoing.</strong> This statement is not a claim of formal WCAG certification or full accessibility conformance.</div>
<h2>Our Approach</h2><p>We aim to provide clear headings, readable contrast, useful image descriptions, visible keyboard focus, keyboard-operable navigation and forms, and responsive pages across screen sizes. We are working to identify and correct barriers.</p>
<h2>Third-Party Content</h2><p>An embedded Google events calendar and other externally provided features may behave differently with assistive technologies; we intend to provide alternative ways to access essential information when practical.</p>
<h2>Report an Accessibility Issue</h2><p>If something is hard to use, contact <a href="mailto:info@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Accessibility%20Feedback">info@gearmotofoundation.org</a>. Please include the page URL and a description of the difficulty, along with any preferred format or alternative. Do not include sensitive medical or financial information.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/contact/">Contact GEAR ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/privacy/">Privacy &amp; Data Use ↗</a></div>
</div></section>
</Base>
